75.m:
Brahmā said:
As he was praising him thus, the one whose banner bears a bull,
glorious, accompanied by Umā and surrounded by Gaṇeśa and the attendants, appeared before him;

The Lord said:
You have asked for the benefit of the three worlds;
now ask, free from all fear, for a boon for your own benefit!

88.m:
Yājñavalkya said:
“The lord of waters is your guru, your father-in-law, and one who acts for your good;
go to him and ask, O king; he will instruct you in what is beneficial.”
